From aa378a4f6928fbce231744467724e59d0c8ec24c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:05:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a model the user said sees is picked though its
 ID carries a namespace colon (#4359)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed

AutoVision never picked a model of a relay whose IDs carry a vendor
namespace (cn:deepseek-v4.1-flash, gateway key 21/cn:…), though the user
had marked every one as taking images in settings.json's modelImages:
smallCands dropped every model whose lowercased ID holds a colon or a
tilde, and the drop came after keep (seesAt) had read the user's answer,
so their word never reached the pick — the pool came out empty and seer()
said no model sees, while naming the model in vision worked.

smallCands now reads the pool's settings once and leaves a model the
user gave an answer about (ImageOverride) in the pool whatever characters
its ID carries: their answer names one of the vendor's models in full,
which is exactly what the colon, the tilde and the nano/lite/image/…
words were guessing at. The shape filters stand for every model they
said nothing of, and the structural ones — a group's, a found group's,
and, on a subscription, what magpie wrote into its agent — stand even
for a model they did name. The searcher's pool reads the same answer:
the filters are one judgment, and a model the user proved real can be
searched with too; a relay is asked to search only where it was before.

Run

- TestAutoVisionPicksANamespacedIDTheUserSaidSees (new) fails on the old
  smallCands with "AutoVision = \"\", want
  relay/cn:deepseek-v4.1-flash, the model the user said sees" and passes
  now; it also holds that with no answer of the user's the model stays
  out, and that their "takes no images" keeps it out.
- go test -tags nogui -count=1 ./internal/gateway/ (whole package).

Fixes #4359

